<title>USA: U.S. banks free rsvs $787 mln/day Aug 13 two weeks.</title>
<headline>U.S. banks free rsvs $787 mln/day Aug 13 two weeks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $787 million per day in the two weeks ended August 13, versus revised free reserves of $546 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $371 million versus $363 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
